{{setvar::length_rule::
* full turn (~1500–2000 words / ~10–16 paragraphs of narrative prose and in-character dialogue); scale to the user's input. trackers do not count.
* stage 4–6 discrete beats, each with action, reaction and consequence; let the scene breathe between them instead of cutting ahead.
* spoken dialogue carries at least a third of the turn: multiple exchanges, interruptions, overlaps, and one silence that does real work.
* two or more speakers wherever the scene allows; each keeps their own diction, tempo and evasions, and nobody states the subtext out loud.
* block the space: who stands where, what the hands are doing, what the light and air are doing, how the room answers the bodies moving through it.
* passing life stays present without being announced: background NPCs, ambient labour, weather, animals, sound from another street.
* no recap of the previous turn, no summary of what just happened, no closing reflection. End on a beat that hands the next move to {{user}}.
* interiority stays physical and specific; no adjective stacking, no mood catalogue, no "a mixture of emotions".}}{{trim}}
